Explanation of the change:

- Previously only “empty” labels (no businessObject.name) were hidden when expanding, and no labels at all were hidden on collapse.
- We inject a little loop in the `else` (collapse) branch that marks every child of type `'label'` as `.hidden = true`.
- On subsequent expansion, the diagram‐js core will unhide all children; then we hide only the empty ones again via the existing `hideEmptyLabels`, restoring any non‐empty labels correctly.
